# New bound keys needed (pinyin as stated):
#   陪臣 (péi chén — a rear vassal: a grandee's household retainer, a vassal's vassal; Zhu Xi 陪臣家臣也; Ma Rong
#     in He Yan 陪重也謂家臣也)
#   庶人 (shù rén — the common people, the multitude without rank; Zhu Xi on 16.2 speaks of 下 'those below'
#     who have no 私議; Kong Anguo 無所非議也)
#   三桓 (sān huán — the Three Huan: the three great houses of Lu, Mengsun (Zhongsun), Shusun and Jisun, all
#     descended from Duke Huan of Lu; Kong Anguo in He Yan 三桓者謂仲孫叔孫季孫也三卿皆出桓公也故曰三桓也;
#     Zhu Xi 三桓三家 — = the 三家 of 3.2)
#   血氣 (xuè qì — blood and breath: the bodily vigour that waxes and wanes with age; Zhu Xi 血氣形之所待以生者
#     血隂而氣陽也)
#   大人 (dà rén — great men: men of high standing and virtue; Zhu Xi 大人聖言皆天命所當畏; He Yan
#     大人即聖人與天地合其德者也)
#   首陽 (shǒu yáng — Shouyang, the mountain where Boyi and Shuqi starved; Zhu Xi 首陽山名; Ma Rong
#     首陽山在河東蒲坂華山之北河曲之中也)
#   陳亢 (chén kàng — Chen Kang, courtesy name Ziqin 子禽; Zhu Xi 亢音剛 'read gāng'; usual reading kàng)
#   伯魚 (bó yú — Bo Yu: Kong Li 鯉, Confucius's son; Ma Rong in He Yan 以為伯魚孔子之子)
#   夫人 (fū rén — the Lady: title of a ruler's wife, used by the ruler and by the people of the state)
#   小童 (xiǎo tóng — 'Little Child': how a ruler's wife names herself, in modesty)
#   小君 (xiǎo jūn — 'Little Lord': a title of the ruler's wife; Kong Anguo in He Yan: a name for the lord's lady,
#     with 寡 before it when speaking to other states, 對異邦謙故曰寡小君)
# New single characters needed (not yet GLOSS keys), with the sense used here:
#   征 zhēng (to march against, to make a punitive campaign; 征伐 16.2), 盖 gài (the edition's form of 蓋:
#   probably, roughly; Zhu Xi's own gloss of the line 大約世數不過如此), 陪 péi (doubled, secondary, attendant;
#   Ma Rong 陪重也 — in 陪臣), 柔 róu (soft, pliant; 善柔 Zhu Xi 工於媚説而不諒, Ma Rong 面柔也), 佚 yì (idle,
#   at ease, dissipated; 佚遊 Zhu Xi 惰慢而惡聞善, Wang Su 出入不知節也), 宴 yàn (a feast, feasting; 宴樂 Zhu Xi
