dict(pas="16.2", w="孔子=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | 曰：「/said | ^天下=tiān xià/(when) the world | 有/has | 道=dào/the Way | 則/then | ^禮/the rites | 樂=yuè/and music | 征=zhēng/(and) campaigns | 伐/and attacks | 自/from | 天子=tiān zǐ/the Son of Heaven | 出；/issue | ^天下=tiān xià/(when) the world | 無/lacks | 道=dào/the Way | 則/then | ^禮/the rites | 樂=yuè/and music | 征=zhēng/(and) campaigns | 伐/and attacks | 自/from | 諸侯=zhū hóu/the feudal lords | 出。/issue | ^自/from | 諸侯=zhū hóu/the feudal lords | 出，/(when they) issue | 盖=gài/likely | 十/(in) ten | 世/generations | 希/rarely | 不/(do they) not | 失/lose (them) | 矣；/(so it is) | ^自/from | 大夫=dà fū/the grandees | 出，/(when they) issue | 五/(in) five | 世/generations | 希/rarely | 不/(do they) not | 失/lose (them) | 矣；/(so it is) | ^陪臣=péi chén/(when) the household retainers//doubled, secondary//subject, retainer | 執/hold | 國/the state's | 命，/commands | 三/(in) three | 世/generations | 希/rarely | 不/(do they) not | 失/lose (them) | 矣。」/(so it is)",
  l="Kongzi said:\n“When the world has the Way, then\nthe rites and music and the campaigns and attacks issue from the Son of Heaven;\nwhen the world lacks the Way, then\nthe rites and music and the campaigns and attacks issue from the feudal lords.\nWhen they issue from the feudal lords, likely in ten generations few fail to lose them;\nwhen they issue from the grandees, in five generations few fail to lose them;\nwhen household retainers hold the state's commands, in three generations few fail to lose them.”",
  i="Kongzi said: “When the world is on the Way, the rites and music, and the making of war on those who do wrong, are ordered by the Son of Heaven. When the world has left the Way, they are ordered by the feudal lords. Once they are in the lords' hands, it will be a rare house that keeps hold of them for as long as ten generations; once they are in the grandees' hands, a rare house that keeps them five; and when the grandees' own retainers take charge of the state's commands, a rare one that keeps them three.”",
  n="孔子曰 'Kongzi said', as in every saying of the Master in this book (see 16.1). 天下有道 / 無道 'the world has / lacks the Way' (as 8.13). 禮樂 'the rites and music', 樂 yuè (as 11.1, 13.3). 征 zhēng is to march against, to bring force to bear on those who have done wrong, and 伐 'to attack'; together, the right of making war. 自…出 'issue from'. 盖 gài is the edition's form of 蓋 'likely, roughly'. 十世希不失矣 'in ten generations, rarely do they not lose (it)': 希 'rare' (Kong Anguo in He Yan: 希少也), 不失 'not lose'. 世 here is a generation of rulers in one house (not Zhu Xi's 'dynasty' of 2.23). 陪臣 péi chén are the retainers of the grandees, a vassal's vassal: Zhu Xi: 陪臣家臣也; Ma Rong in He Yan: 陪 is 'doubled' (陪重也). 國命 'the state's commands'. Zhu Xi: by the institutions of the former kings, the lords could not alter the rites and music nor take campaigns into their own hands (先王之制諸侯不得變禮樂專征伐); the further one goes against principle, the faster it is lost (逆理愈甚則其失之愈速), and the numbers of generations are roughly no more than these (大約世數不過如此). He Yan's commentators count them out in history: Kong Anguo, that after King You was killed and King Ping moved east the Zhou grew weak and the lords made their own rites and music, and in Lu from Duke Yin to Duke Zhao ten generations passed before Duke Zhao lost his government and died in exile at Ganhou; and that from Ji Wenzi, who first took the government, to Ji Huanzi was five generations, when Huanzi was made prisoner by his own retainer Yang Hu; Ma Rong, that the Yang were retainers of the Ji for three generations until Hu fled to Qi. Kongzi's words run on past Zhu Xi's comment; the next two units are left unquoted."),
dict(w="^天下=tiān xià/(when) the world | 有/has | 道=dào/the Way | 則/then | ^政/government | 不/does not | 在/lie | 大夫。=dà fū/with the grandees",
  l="When the world has the Way, then\ngovernment does not lie with the grandees.",
  i="When the world is on the Way, government is not in the hands of the grandees.",
  n="Still Kongzi, unquoted. 政 'government'; 不在大夫 'is not with the grandees'. Zhu Xi: that is, they may not take the government into their own hands (言不得專政). Kong Anguo in He Yan: its control comes from the ruler (制之由君也)."),
dict(w="^天下=tiān xià/(when) the world | 有/has | 道=dào/the Way | 則/then | ^庶人=shù rén/the common people//many, multitude//person | 不/do not | 議。/find fault",
  l="When the world has the Way, then\nthe common people do not find fault.",
  i="When the world is on the Way, the common people have no complaints to make about their government.",
  n="Still Kongzi, unquoted. 庶人 shù rén 'the common people', the many who hold no rank. 議 'to debate, to criticize'. Zhu Xi: when those above make no failures in government, those below have no private criticism — it is not that their mouths are clamped so that they dare not speak (上無失政則下無私議非箝其口使不敢言也); and of the whole chapter: it treats in general the course of the world (此章通論天下之勢). Kong Anguo in He Yan: they have nothing to find fault with (無所非議也)."),
# ---------------- 16.3 ----------------
dict(pas="16.3", w="孔子=kǒng zǐ/Kongzi | 曰：「/said | ^禄/salary (the bestowing of it) | 之/(makes 'salary leaving the ducal house' one phrase) | 去=qù/has gone from | 公/the ducal | 室，/house | 五/(for) five | 世/generations | 矣；/now | ^政/government | 逮/has come down | 於/to | 大夫=dà fū/the grandees | 四/(for) four | 世/generations | 矣；/now | ^故/and so | 夫=fú/those | 三桓=sān huán/Three Huan (houses)//three//Huan (Duke Huan of Lu) | 之/'s | 子/sons | 孫，/and grandsons | 微/are dwindling | 矣。」/(so it is)",
  l="Kongzi said:\n“Salary has been gone from the ducal house five generations now;\ngovernment has come down to the grandees four generations now;\nand so those sons and grandsons of the Three Huan are dwindling.”",
  i="Kongzi said: “For five generations the giving of rank and pay has been out of the ducal house's hands, and for four generations government has rested with the grandees. That is why the descendants of the three Huan houses are themselves now in decline.”",
  n="禄 'salary', here the ruler's power to grant rank and pay: Zheng Xuan in He Yan says rank and salary no longer came from the ruler (爵禄不從君出). 之 makes 禄之去公室 'salary's leaving the ducal house' one phrase; 去 qù 'to go from'; 公室 'the ducal house'. 逮 dài 'to reach' (Zhu Xi: 逮及也). 夫 fú 'those', pointing (Zhu Xi: 夫音扶). 三桓 sān huán, the Three Huan, are the three great houses of Lu, the Three Families of 3.2: Kong Anguo in He Yan: Zhongsun, Shusun and Jisun, all three ministers descended from Duke Huan, hence the name (三卿皆出桓公也故曰三桓也); the Zhongsun later took the name Meng. 微 'small', so 'to dwindle'. Zhu Xi counts the generations: from the death of Duke Wen, when Prince Sui killed (the heir) Chi and set up Duke Xuan, the ruler of Lu lost his government, through Cheng, Xiang, Zhao and Ding, five dukes in all; from Ji Wuzi the Ji began to hold the government of the state, through Daozi, Pingzi and Huanzi, four generations in all, and then (Huanzi) was seized by his retainer Yang Hu. This, he says, was worked out from the previous chapter's account (此以前章之説推之而知其當然也); this chapter speaks of Lu alone, and he suspects both were said in Duke Ding's time (疑與前章皆定公時語). He quotes Su Shi: when the lords take over the rites and the campaigns they should grow strong, yet Lu lost its government; when government comes down to the grandees they should grow strong, yet the Three Huan dwindled — why? Strength comes from security, and security from a settled division between above and below (强生於安安生於上下之分定); now lords and grandees alike overrode those above them, so had nothing to command those below with, and none lasted. Zheng Xuan counts differently: the five generations from Xiangzhong's killing of Chi to Duke Ding, and the four as Wenzi, Wuzi, Daozi and Pingzi (文子武子悼子平子也). Variant: He Yan's text reads 政逮大夫, without 於."),
